# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inner Datum — .gitignore
# This repo is PUBLIC. Everything below is either secret, huge, generated,
# or licensed such that we must not redistribute it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets. Never commit. --------------------------------------------------
# The Discord client secret and OAuth tokens live here. A leaked client secret
# lets anyone impersonate the activity; rotate immediately if it ever lands in
# a commit (deleting the file later does NOT remove it from git history).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
config.local.json

# --- Third-party reference source. Do NOT commit. ---------------------------
# reference/t-engine4 is a ~330 MB sparse clone of T-Engine4/ToME (GPL-3.0),
# kept locally as a porting reference only. It is upstream's code, not ours:
# anyone who needs it should clone it themselves. See docs/tome-port.md.
reference/

# --- Player data. Contains Discord user IDs — personal data, not ours to publish.
data/
saves/
*.save.json
backups/

# --- Node / build --------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.eslintcache

# --- THE ART. Not published. ------------------------------------------------
# The entire art tree is excluded: sprites, icons, atlases, the generated
# manifest and the prop metadata alongside them. It is All Rights Reserved and
# is NOT distributed with this repository. See ASSETS-LICENSE.md.
#
# The files stay on disk and the game keeps running locally. Only git is told
# to look away.
#
# This is a whole-directory rule on purpose. A rule listing subfolders would
# quietly start tracking the next folder someone adds, and the failure mode is
# publishing art nobody meant to publish. If you need a file in here committed,
# it is almost certainly in the wrong directory — move it, do not un-ignore it.
#
# What a clone does instead: `npm run assets` generates 64 of the 111 sprites
# procedurally, and ASSETS-REQUIRED.md lists the other 47 with their exact
# dimensions. Missing sprites draw as fallback boxes; nothing crashes.
client/public/assets/

# --- Logs / runtime --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
pids/
*.pid

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
*.swp

# ===========================================================================
# ADDED AFTER THE PUBLIC-RELEASE AUDIT
# Everything above is unchanged and still correct. This section covers the
# gaps that audit found. Rule of thumb: if you have to stop and think about
# whether a file is safe to commit, it isn't — add it here first and argue
# afterwards.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Other people's personal data (the biggest gap) ------------------------
# docs/hosting.md § 8.4 tells you to create a file of ~10 friends' Discord
# snowflakes. Nothing above was stopping it from being committed.
# Ship config/allowlist.example.json instead.
config/allowlist.json
config/gm.json
!config/*.example.json

# architecture.md § 6 dumps a serialised world (every player in it) on
# unhandledRejection; hosting.md § 7 writes an append-only action log.
# Both carry Discord user IDs.
crashdumps/
snapshots/
*.ndjson

# --- Key material beyond *.pem / *.key -------------------------------------
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
secrets/
*.local.json
!*.example.json

# --- Hosting credentials ---------------------------------------------------
# These are supposed to live outside the repo entirely (hosting.md § 8.8).
# This block is the seatbelt, not the plan.
# Caddy's data dir holds the ACME account key and every issued private key.
caddy/data/
caddy/config/
Caddyfile.local
# cloudflared (fallback path). cert.pem is account-scoped: it can create
# tunnels and DNS records across all your zones. Most dangerous file on the box.
.cloudflared/
cloudflared-config.yml
*-tunnel.json
cert.pem

# --- Untraced audio. Do not "restore the missing music". -------------------
# art-pipeline.md § 7: 36 tracks with no licence file and no provenance note.
# On a public repo that is a liability, not a to-do. See ASSETS-LICENSE.md § 8.
assets/audio/
client/public/assets/audio/
*.mp3
*.m4a

# --- Local agent / editor state --------------------------------------------
# .claude/settings.json (project hooks) and CLAUDE.md ARE committed.
# Anything machine-local is not — see NEXUS-PLAN.md § Task 0 for why this
# matters more here than in most repos.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/logs/
.claude/state/
CLAUDE.local.md
NEXUS/state/
NEXUS/logs/
NEXUS/changelog/

# .vscode/settings.shared.json (negated above) is a name no tool reads —
# VS Code only ever loads settings.json. Un-ignore the real one.
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# --- Local binaries --------------------------------------------------------
# caddy.exe / cloudflared.exe / nssm.exe belong outside the repo. This catches
# an accidental drop-in.
bin/
*.exe
*.msi

# --- Node, continued -------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: package-lock.json IS committed. Do not add it here.
dist-ssr/
.node_repl_history
*.tgz
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/releases
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Build reports ---------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded: the art tree is now excluded wholesale further up this file, so
# the assets are no longer committed and the "zero churn on rebuild" argument
# for committing them no longer applies. The throwaway report stays ignored.
tools/*-report.json

# --- OS / editor, continued ------------------------------------------------
.AppleDouble
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ===========================================================================
# PRIVATE DESIGN + PLANNING DOCS — local only, never published
# ===========================================================================
# Decision: the public repo carries CODE and LICENCE files only, plus a short
# README and the two OSS furniture files. The planning and design material
# stays on this machine.
#
# These files are NOT deleted and NOT secret — they are the working notes for
# the project and remain the source of truth locally. They are simply not the
# public face of the repo.
#
# If you add a new design doc, it lands in docs/ and is ignored automatically.

/PLAN.md
/DECISIONS.md
/NEXUS-PLAN.md
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
docs/
tools/README.md
NEXUS/

# Explicitly committed, despite the rules above. Do not let a broad *.md rule
# swallow these — they are licence files or required repo furniture:
#   LICENSE  COPYING  NOTICE  ASSETS-LICENSE.md  THIRD_PARTY.md
#   README.md  SECURITY.md  CONTRIBUTING.md
!/ASSETS-LICENSE.md
!/THIRD_PARTY.md
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md

# Working scratch that accumulates next to the docs
/contact_*.png
/scratch_*.png
*.contact.png

# ===========================================================================
# PERSONAL INFRASTRUCTURE — local only, never published
# ===========================================================================
# This repo is public and must contain CODE and LICENCES only. The files below
# are this author's specific deployment: they name a home hostname that
# resolves to a residential IP, a machine on a private LAN, a mapped drive, and
# an absolute path carrying a Windows username. None of it is useful to anyone
# else, and publishing it would hand a stranger the address of a PC in
# somebody's house.
#
# They remain on disk and keep working. Only git is told to look away.

# A GLOB, not a list of filenames. Every deploy script names the host it
# deploys to — an address, a drive, a machine on a LAN — so the rule has to
# cover the one somebody writes next, not just the two that exist today.
# Getting this wrong publishes a home address, and it only has to happen once.
tools/deploy-*.ps1
.githooks/post-commit
tools/discord/

# The real Caddyfile names the live host. deploy/Caddyfile.example is the
# published, generic one.
deploy/Caddyfile
